BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.77 Tm (The most expensive failure is a full closure triggered by pattern spend. Just Money Ish describes the trigger precisely:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.55 Tm (buying the same item weekly or monthly gets the account flagged, restricted, or closed because it reads as money) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.32 Tm (laundering. Gift cards turned into money orders are the textbook case [Cm-vEtFQnC0 @ 00:02:26]. The same speaker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 496.10 Tm (adds that the closure lowers the credit score and forfeits the points. In the companion breakdown, the channel warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.87 Tm (that heavy cycling can bring lowered limits, frozen accounts, and closure of every account held with that issuer. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.65 Tm (names four to five cycles a month at Capital One as the line that gets people closed [u8QBKSzn5K8 @ 00:02:10]. RJ) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.42 Tm (Financial flags a mechanical trap for anyone freeing up room mid-cycle: ACH payments can be unwound, so room that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 435.20 Tm (looks open on the account can vanish when the payment reverses [HCkT2XqTvms @ 00:07:01]. RJ also notes that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.97 Tm (Amex and Citi credit payments instantly, but prepaying never raises the limit itself. Jack McColl adds a points-specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.75 Tm (trap on exits: closing your last Membership Rewards card zeroes the points balance [SNCeMDvlJsQ @ 00:11:25]. That) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.52 Tm (means any Amex shutdown or voluntary cancellation should happen only after the rewards are spent or another) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.30 Tm (Membership Rewards card stays open. Together, these failures turn a limit-building tactic into lost credit, lost points,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 359.07 Tm (and a damaged profile with that bank.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.85 Tm (Denials are the second trap, and they usually trace back to low usage or bad timing. Naam Wynn admits he was denied) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.62 Tm (on a card he rarely used, calling the request an attempt to "stroke my ego." His conclusion: "there's really no reason to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.40 Tm (extend a higher credit limit to someone who doesn't use their credit card" [6KiaTyIQOCQ @ 00:04:35]. Just Money Ish) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 298.17 Tm (reports the same pattern at Capital One at scale: "I've literally seen dozens of people get denied for a credit limit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.95 Tm (increase with Capital One because they're just not simply using their card enough" [Cm-vEtFQnC0 @ 00:00:19]. Bella) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.72 Tm (Sloan Enterprises warns that repeated denials lengthen the cool-off and give banks a reason to cut limits. She reframes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.50 Tm (the adverse-action letter as a work order: "They're actually the bank telling you exactly what to fix" [2sUP7XrGRgM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.27 Tm (@ 00:07:12]. Stephen Smith sets the retry clock after a denial at three months when the pull was soft and six months) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 222.05 Tm (when it was hard. He also flags that USAA still hard-pulls while Barclays has moved to soft [RY2Q9yq3v3E @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.82 Tm (00:14:36]. Naam Wynn's own adverse-action map lines up with that clock. Too new means wait, too many inquiries) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.60 Tm (means stop applying for three to six months, and a delinquency means a 12-month wait before asking again. Firing off) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.37 Tm (requests without fixing the coded reason only stacks more denials.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 161.15 Tm (The economics checks cut against the pure limit-maximizing playbook. ProudMoney cites Boston Fed research) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.92 Tm (showing that utilization percentage stays constant as limits change, meaning balances scale up with the line. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.70 Tm (channel adds that people who revolve balances pay 15-20% more, and tells anyone tempted to spend more by a bigger) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.47 Tm (limit to decline the increase [IrfC1PHQGVQ @ 00:07:22]. Limits also move in both directions. ProudMoney points to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.25 Tm (roughly 40% limit cuts during 2008-09, and Cal Barton warns that X1 cut limits by more than $30K [D6bPd67bgps @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 85.02 Tm (00:11:01]. Personal utilization also bleeds into business lines. Business Credit Workshop says "Amex is very in tune) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 69.80 Tm (with your personal credit utilization." A maxed personal Blue depressed their Business Gold limit, and paying it to $0) Tj ET
